  message: "Decision artifact landed: ADR-0043 (Stage-Ordering Contract for run_behavior_map), PR #4212. The contract — target six-phase DAG + the five conflict resolutions C1-C5 — is now recorded and indexed in docs/adr/README.md. Adversarially reviewed (3 lenses vs cli.py + the rulings; ship_with_nits): all four ordering defects C1-C4 and the five C5 finalizers were code-verified against the live run_behavior_map; §7 was corrected to distinguish the existing validate_ir STAGE (the C1 defect) from ADR-0037's not-yet-implemented referential-integrity/FK predicate. This WI now carries the IMPLEMENTATION (Wave 2): the reorder owns seam (a) and sequences AFTER identity's seam-(b) scope-stack rewrite; the finalize stage is carried by run-lifecycle:F1 and co-designed before its consumers implement. META-jalur stays violated until run_signature, edge finalization, validation, and the compact/budget projections all route through the one finalize stage with a serialization round-trip property test passing (ADR-0043 §6/§8)."  # d8c5
